WEBVTT

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.320
Hey! They're not open yet, Ko.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.390
Huh?

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.990
Oh, they open at 10.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.650
Who knew?

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:23.730
Don't "who knew" me.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.840
You've been coming here for how long now?

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.590
Let's see, it's been about... Hmm...

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:31.980
Ko!

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.760
Heya!

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.350
Don't "heya" me.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:39.670
Didn't I tell you that grade-schoolers should show high schoolers a little more respect?

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.390
<i>High schooler</i> Ko, then.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.600
This is your first time meeting her, right?

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.290
This here is...

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:56.940
Tsukishima...

00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:59.380
Wakaba.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.950
Let's play catch, Waka!

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.680
I'm playing with Ko now, so let's go later.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.900
When's "later"?

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.660
When Ko goes back home.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.560
Go home already, will you?

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.030
Aoba!

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:20.550
Morning.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:24.340
Look who finally decided to wake up.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.470
Where's Momiji?

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.950
She went off somewhere with Ko just now.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:33.730
Give these to Ko to eat when he comes back, will you, Ichiyo?

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.570
Okay.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:38.310
Geez.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:41.670
What's with this family and spoiling that guy so much?

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:43.800
You're just the odd one out.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.510
You really loved Wakaba, didn't you?

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:53.350
And Ko would always have your beloved Wakaba all to himself.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:56.800
I wouldn't mind it so much if he had it together.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.890
He's rude, irresponsible, slow to wake up,

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:02.740
and his room's always a mess!

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:06.560
He wears shirts with holes in them and couldn't care less.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.570
Everything he does ticks me—

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.050
I see.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:16.300
You guys are alike.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.060
You and Ko, I mean.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:27.960
I see.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.750
You thought she was Wakaba, huh?

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.390
Yeah, it almost knocked me off my feet.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.140
She's in the fifth grade right now.

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.690
Same as when Wakaba died.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:01.590
She was only that big, huh?

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.710
Yeah.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.630
I'm hungry now, Ko.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.390
Let's go home.

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:09.220
Okay.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:11.120
Thanks for playing with me, Mister!

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:16.060
The pleasure's all mine. Been a while since I had some good exercise.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.570
Thanks for letting me borrow this.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:22.440
You're quite impressive, Missy.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:27.410
I never thought a grade-schooler could throw a ball like that. Not to mention a girl!

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:32.740
Ao used to throw way better when she was my age, right?

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:33.410
I'd say so.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:36.480
By "Ao" do you mean...

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:40.250
the pitcher from that middle school baseball team?

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.450
Do you know her, Mister?

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.700
Oh yes.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:47.750
The boy from the liquor store right here has let me in on a few things.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:50.670
He tells me all about the baseball team.

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:52.940
Are you sure you're okay, old man?

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:56.680
Don't blame us if you pass out from fatigue, okay?

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:01.910
It's nothing a little drink can't fix.

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.820
Well then, liquor store's son,

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.410
say hi to your father for me.

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:09.580
Who was that old guy?

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:12.020
He's a regular at the store.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.620
I don't know much about him,

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.960
but I see him show up at the store once a week, getting all excited while talking about booze.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.860
I thought I smelled booze on him.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:23.760
Let's go back already, Ko!

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:25.140
Sure thing.

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:38.460
I was supposed to have lunch with my granddaughter at noon, right?

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:39.390
Yes, sir.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.080
Such a nice day.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.840
I'm home!

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:55.230
And I'm hungry! Do we have any snacks?

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:59.160
Here, go eat these with the guys.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.360
Did Ao get up yet?

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:06.420
She's working out in her room.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.270
I told her to take a break if she's feeling tired,

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.780
but she said no, and said she's really upset about something.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.210
Upset?

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.120
Could it be Azuma?

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.230
She doesn't like to lose.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:24.890
Damn it!

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.960
Hey, we should be getting back soon.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:30.750
Sorry, just a little longer.

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:36.370
He's at it again.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:37.240
"Again"?

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:38.360
Yeah.

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:42.220
He's been at it ever since his home run record got broken.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:45.210
Exactly the same...

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:47.530
What do you mean?

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:48.780
You guys don't like to lose.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:04.200
Since when did ping pong become an outdoor sport?

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:08.950
Ever since the acting principal said it should be, of course.

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:15.440
I must thank you for listening to my unreasonable requests,

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:19.040
Acting Principal.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.170
There's no need to thank me.

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:25.020
As long as you show me the results within three years, that is.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.120
In exchange...

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:29.400
I know.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:35.030
It is vital for someone like me to keep showing results in order to survive,

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:38.800
if only to raise my own value as a coach.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:41.690
That reminds me,

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:46.610
I heard you were planning to have a scrimmage against the Prefab team before the Summer Tournament.

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:49.470
Are you planning to promote a few players to first string?

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:53.900
As I've told you before,

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:57.350
there aren't any worthwhile players on the team outside of the players I've brought in.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:01.650
However, I must say that there are a few amateurs who seem to be getting the wrong impression.

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:06.870
I thought it'd be a good idea to silence the fertilizers'
whining before they make a big deal of it

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:11.930
by showing them exactly how a real team plays.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.140
I see.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:17.140
So you're picking on the weak? I like it.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:19.860
I hope you come and observe as well, Principal.

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:23.320
Don't forget the "Acting." I'm the Acting Principal.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:40.760
The twelfth-graders were out running in the rain.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.460
They sure are fired up.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.900
This is going to be their last summer, after all.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:52.270
I wonder if they really think they'll make first string if they stand out during the scrimmage.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:54.710
They probably wouldn't be doing this if they didn't.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:57.200
What do you have there?

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:01.810
This is our starting roster for the scrimmage against the first-string team.

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:05.620
First batter: center field, Tsuneki.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.550
Second batter: shortstop, Kayama.

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:09.850
Third batter: second baseman, Sekiguchi.

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:11.820
Fourth batter: third baseman, Makihara.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:13.720
Fifth batter: pitcher, Me.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:15.620
Sixth batter: left fielder, Miya.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:17.750
Seventh batter: catcher, Akaishi.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.950
Eighth batter: first baseman, Nakanishi.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.870
Ninth batter: right fielder, Iwai.

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:25.800
The twelfth-graders will be batting from first to fourth.

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:29.170
But we won't really be going on the offensive until you come up and bat fifth.

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:31.710
We'll need you to get on base somehow

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:34.780
and Miya, the best bunter on the team, will sacrifice you to second.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:38.110
After that, Nakanishi or I will get you home.

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:42.500
I can't think of any other order that can get us runs against the first-string team.

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:47.410
We'll get their guard down with our first four batters and leave them open for attack.

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:48.490
Pretty good, huh?

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:53.870
Maybe, but is this really up to us tenth-graders to decide?

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:55.570
What do you mean, us?

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:59.000
Coach Maeno was the one who came up with this.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:04.270
I was actually waiting for Senda to be relegated back to the Farm,

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:08.450
but it seems like he's holding on by a thread.

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:12.000
I don't think he'll go very far as a pitcher,

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:15.150
but with his footwork, his defensive skills, and that arm...

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:19.960
I think he'll make a good showboating shortstop.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:21.590
Don't you think so, Akaishi?

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:23.290
I agree.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:25.620
Sadly, there's nothing we can do about it.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:28.270
Let's go with the players we have on that roster for now.

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:29.730
Kitamura.

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:34.410
Show me a good dream, okay?

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:52.990
Out of the way!

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:55.930
It's hard enough practicing in such a small area like this.

00:11:55.930 --> 00:12:00.290
Go run off somewhere when we
twelfth-graders are practicing, will you?

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:02.270
Let's make it to the first string!

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:05.210
Prefab, fight!

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:07.210
Prefab, fight...

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.610
Miya, Iwai, what's with you guys today?

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:12.470
I'm ready to do my best, Akaishi.

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:16.050
Let's show them exactly what the Prefab team's made of.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:18.480
Yeah.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.940
We're counting on you, Kitamura.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:23.790
You're our beacon of hope.

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:27.110
Prefab, fight!

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:28.990
Prefab, fight!

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:32.320
They're all fired up, huh?

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:33.790
Yeah.

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:37.570
But either way, we'll have to know more about our enemy before we pick a fight with them.

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:51.710
Let's take a little break, Miya.

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:52.570
Yeah.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:58.990
Okay, let's give it another shot.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:00.070
Yup.

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:07.800
What are they up to now?

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:09.230
Watch the hands!

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.680
They've got good batters, as we figured.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.680
Yeah.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:31.320
I guess they're not "baseball transfer students" for nothing, huh?

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:39.300
That's Kamikawa, who we predict will be pitching first for the first-stringers.

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:44.340
And just as I thought...

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:52.080
He's an annoying pitcher who will toss change-ups every now and then.

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:53.880
<i>Change-ups, huh?</i>

00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:59.340
Is that the best fastball you can throw?

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:03.820
You haven't changed much since last fall.

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:09.770
I expected your speed to improve by at least 4-5 km/h before the summer,

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:11.260
but I guess I hoped for too much.

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:12.030
What did you say?!

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:15.700
Only luck can save you if that's all you can throw.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:18.470
You'll need to throw 5 km/h faster if you want to make it to Koshien.

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:24.620
I joined this team because of you, Kishibe, and Miki.

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:29.180
You three and that coach make for the highest probability of getting to Koshien.

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:31.580
Don't you dare make a fool out of me.

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:41.590
Four km/h to go.

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:45.930
I can't hear what they're saying,

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:48.870
but I don't think teamwork is one of their strengths.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:53.300
You can't really say much about our relationship with the seniors, either.

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:55.050
I guess not.

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:58.210
But I gotta ask...

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:58.210
What?

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:03.480
Is that guy really a high schooler?

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:09.090
Make sure these balls sparkle for us, okay, Chubby?

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:11.500
Sure!

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:18.700
She always works hard without a single frown on her face. What a nice girl.

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:22.470
I didn't see her when we were in
middle school. Transfer student, right?

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:25.900
Yeah, she'd been living abroad in America, apparently.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:31.180
Now that you mention it, we have another one of those "lived abroad" girls around.

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.610
Right, Ko?

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:36.250
What's wrong? You're spacing out.

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:37.980
Nothing.

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:40.450
Oh yeah, did you see this?

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:44.070
These are the profiles for the transfer students on the first-string team.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:44.660
Yeah.

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:49.460
It's full of guys who really stood out in the little and senior leagues.

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:51.230
Of course it is.

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:53.760
For that coach to basically drag them here, they'd have to.

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:55.610
Yeah...

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:03.670
I'm home.

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:08.040
Welcome back!

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:10.010
Hey, you idiot son of mine!

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:14.520
Geez. Since when did our liquor store become a bar?

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:19.660
So, I hear you guys are playing a scrimmage against the first-string team in two days?

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:23.560
Dad, what did I tell you about telling people unnecessary things?

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:25.600
How about it? Do you think you can win?

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.600
We'd flip the school on its head if we won.

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:32.340
Then just flip it over.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:36.040
You don't like that coach or the vice principal, right?

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:40.710
He's not the vice principal. He's the "acting principal," or so he says.

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:42.170
Beat 'em, beat 'em!

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:44.110
Make 'em foam at the mouth in frustration!

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:45.440
Foam?

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:48.010
All right, that calls for a bottle of beer!

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:49.330
Yeah!

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:51.020
Froth, froth! Look, I'm pouring the head!

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:51.020
Good one!

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:56.730
Well, that all depends on how our ace performs.  Right?

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:04.500
Hey, Ko.

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:06.500
Is Aoba here?

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:12.840
I think she's over at the house.

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:14.180
Oh, okay.

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:19.470
You don't see that every day.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:21.820
Ko's looking for <i>Aoba</i>?

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:25.760
You want something from me?

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.160
Come with me for a bit.

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:40.490
Come on, where are you taking me?

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:58.420
Let me hear what you think.

00:17:58.420 --> 00:17:59.520
Huh?

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:02.860
I've never actually pitched in a real game,

00:18:02.860 --> 00:18:05.530
so I have no idea if I'm doing this right.

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:11.870
Plus, Akaishi and Nakanishi will never say anything to make me lose my confidence.

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:13.790
I get it.

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:15.670
You're nervous about your debut game, aren't you?

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:17.670
As if.

00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:21.350
We're playing against a team with elite players from all around the country.

00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:24.620
I'm going to get hammered, no question about it.

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:28.320
The real question is whether I'll be able to even make it a game.

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:31.090
You're rolling over pretty quickly.

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:33.290
Can you see the ball?

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:35.330
Sure I can.

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:38.030
Then here I go.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.740
Come on!

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:10.260
What do you think?

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.930
I guess it's not bad.

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:17.970
Really?

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:20.700
All right!

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:23.770
Wait, what are you getting all happy for?

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:27.230
I only said it's "not bad."

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:28.480
Then it's good.

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:32.950
A "not bad" from you is the best compliment I could expect.

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:39.190
All right, it'll work out somehow.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.110
Oh yeah.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:42.760
If I manage to hold the first-string team to ten runs,

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:44.820
treat me to the Napolitan over at Clover Café.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:47.680
It's got to be cooked by Ichiyo, of course.

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:48.770
See ya.

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:50.340
Five runs.

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:51.300
Huh?

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:53.670
Make it five runs.

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:55.120
Tch.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.160
No fair.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:04.200
No fair for who?

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:27.840
It's finally time.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:31.280
I think the liquor store's son was on the third base side.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:36.520
What the hell's "P" supposed to mean?

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:38.070
Who cares.

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:42.620
More importantly, why are all the people sitting on the first base side?

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:44.890
They even have the brass band playing.

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:49.140
Ever since the Acting Principal said they should, of course.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:53.270
Hold on a moment, Missy!

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:54.300
Yes?

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:58.370
It seems you can only watch today's game from the first base side.

00:20:58.370 --> 00:20:59.360
Huh?

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:00.770
What's going on?

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:04.210
Don't ask me...

00:21:04.690 --> 00:21:06.410
This is their roster.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:08.880
First batter: center fielder, Miki.

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:10.890
Second batter: right fielder, Onoda.

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:12.990
Third batter: shortstop, Kishibe.

00:21:12.990 --> 00:21:15.130
Fourth batter: first baseman, Azuma.

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:16.980
Fifth batter: third baseman, Kubo.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:19.220
Sixth batter: catcher, Takizawa.

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:21.240
Seventh batter: second baseman, Ishiguro.

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:23.100
Eight batter: left fielder, Ogura.

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:24.360
Ninth batter: pitcher...

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:25.400
Huh?

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:28.040
Who's their ninth batter again?

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:12.370
<i>Now hold up!</i>

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:14.590
<i>You guys have to do better than that, Senpais.</i>

00:23:14.590 --> 00:23:18.610
<i>Don't get so cocky just because you're pitching for the first string, you bastard!</i>

00:23:18.610 --> 00:23:19.450
<i>How scary!</i>

00:23:19.450 --> 00:23:21.350
<i>That would have been a home run if you had actually hit it.</i>

00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:24.250
<i>The first-string team's attack will begin with Miki, their center fielder.</i>

00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:28.390
<i>Overall he's deft with the bat, can handle any pitch and likes to hit to the opposite field.</i>

00:23:28.390 --> 00:23:31.360
<i>Seems like you've got a considerable amount of data on us.</i>

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:33.980
<i>Next time, on Cross Game Episode Nine:</i>

00:23:33.980 --> 00:23:35.690
<i>Let's Do This!</i>

00:23:35.690 --> 00:23:38.970
<i>That's the kind of fastball I wanted you to have, Kamikawa.</i>
